Relevant columns & their potential usage  
• "body": contains the full‑text on which the article vector has to be built.  
• "id": unique identifier that must be returned for the final top‑10 list.  
• "date": publication date that must be returned.  
• "title": article title that must be returned.  
• "word": token string appearing both in WORD_FREQUENCIES and GLOVE_VECTORS – used for weighting and for obtaining the GloVe vector.  
• "frequency": corpus frequency needed for the 0.4‑power weighting.  
• "vector": 300‑dimensional GloVe embedding used to build every article / query vector.  

Typical conditions one will later employ  
• Filter "body" (or "title") with ILIKE '%epigenetic%' / '%autism%' etc. to narrow down candidate papers.  
• Join WORD_FREQUENCIES and GLOVE_VECTORS on "word" to obtain both frequency and vector.  
• Tokenise "body" with SPLIT(), LOWER(), REGEXP_REPLACE() to remove punctuation / stop‑words (not shown in these exploratory queries).  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL statements – each limited to 20 rows, with increasing complexity – to familiarise with the content needed before building the final similarity computation.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Quick look at basic article metadata.
SELECT "id", "date", "title"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Inspect a few full article bodies together with their titles.
SELECT "id", "title", "body"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Distinct list of available publication dates (earliest 20) to understand time span.
SELECT DISTINCT "date"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
ORDER BY "date"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Articles whose body already contains ‘epigenetic’ (fuzzy search).
SELECT "id", "date", "title"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
WHERE LOWER("body") ILIKE '%epigenetic%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Examine some low‑frequency words (rarest first) – useful for weighting checks.
SELECT "word", "frequency"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_FREQUENCIES
ORDER BY "frequency" ASC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Pull the GloVe vectors for the main query tokens.
SELECT "word", "vector"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.GLOVE_VECTORS
WHERE "word" IN ('epigenetics', 'cerebral', 'organoids', 'autism', 'spectrum', 'disorders')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Check how many query words have both a frequency and a GloVe vector.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS tokens_present
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.GLOVE_VECTORS g
JOIN WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_FREQUENCIES f
      ON g."word" = f."word"
WHERE g."word" IN ('epigenetics', 'cerebral', 'organoids', 'autism', 'spectrum', 'disorders');
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Join GloVe with frequency for any word beginning with ‘neuro’ (sample 20).
SELECT g."word",
       f."frequency",
       g."vector"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.GLOVE_VECTORS g
JOIN WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_FREQUENCIES f
      ON g."word" = f."word"
WHERE g."word" ILIKE 'neuro%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Estimate token count of bodies (simple whitespace split) to gauge article length.
SELECT "id",
       "title",
       ARRAY_SIZE(SPLIT(LOWER("body"))) AS token_cnt
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Sample full records for articles that mention ‘autism’ or ‘organoid’ to inspect content quality.
SELECT "id", "date", "title", "body"
FROM WORD_VECTORS_US.WORD_VECTORS_US.NATURE
WHERE LOWER("body") ILIKE '%autism%' OR LOWER("body") ILIKE '%organoid%'
LIMIT 20;
```
